Falsifies `system_tests::user::raw_mode_tests::a_copy_badged_as_stdin_reads_the_typed_line_and_nothing_else`.

Architecture: aarch64

The defect: the terminal serves a `STDIN_BADGE` copy its whole surface, as it served every badged
copy before milestone 709 (a graphical terminal session on the no-keyboard arm holds only the raw
half of the boot discipline) narrowed the raw reader's. `jig`'s standard input could then type a line
the shell runs, print, or switch the terminal's mode.

Expected to fail: the assertion that a stdin holder's `OPERATION_BYTES` is refused.

**Re-cut 2026-10-24 (UTC) by maintainer/terminal-quiesce-from-supervisor-only**, when the serve
loop's allowlist moved into `line_editor::proto::admits`. Same defect, `STDIN_BADGE => true`
there. Replayed red on aarch64 the same day, at "a stdin holder's OPERATION_BYTES was served"
(`raw_mode_tests.rs:553`).

diff --git a/crates/line_editor/src/proto.rs b/crates/line_editor/src/proto.rs
index 98a5aff3c..695c42bcb 100644
--- a/crates/line_editor/src/proto.rs
+++ b/crates/line_editor/src/proto.rs
@@ -188,7 +188,7 @@ pub const fn admits(badge: u64, operation: u64) -> bool {
     match badge {
         0 => !matches!(operation, OPERATION_READ_LINE_BYTES | OPERATION_QUIESCE),
         RAW_ONLY_BADGE => matches!(operation, OPERATION_RAWMODE | OPERATION_READRAW),
-        STDIN_BADGE => operation == OPERATION_READ_LINE_BYTES,
+        STDIN_BADGE => true,
         SUPERVISOR_BADGE => operation == OPERATION_QUIESCE,
         _ => false,
     }
